Katana Runtime License (rt/) — DRAFT, awaiting Ghost's approval (status line below)

Copyright (c) 2026 Paul Jensen ("Ghost"). All rights reserved.

This folder (rt/) is the Katana runtime: the Java library that a migrated program links against so
that it behaves as the original COBOL did (records as bytes, COBOL numerics, PERFORM semantics,
file verbs, SORT, CALL). It ships inside every migrated suite Katana produces. Its terms differ from
the rest of this repository (see /LICENSE) in one respect: each customer receives a grant to the
copy inside their own suite. These are those terms (theGhost.md, R-002).

1. No general license. Except as granted in section 2 to a named Licensee, no license is granted to
   use, copy, modify, distribute or run this runtime, commercially or otherwise.

2. Per-customer grant. When Katana delivers a migrated suite to a customer under a written
   engagement, that customer (the "Licensee", named in the engagement's schedule) receives a
   perpetual, worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive license to:
   (a) run, copy and modify the copy of this runtime delivered inside that suite, for the purpose of
       running, maintaining and further developing that suite and the programs Katana migrated for
       the Licensee;
   (b) distribute that copy only as part of that suite, within the Licensee's own organization and
       to contractors working on the Licensee's behalf, who are bound by these terms.
   No recurring fee is owed for the grant. The grant survives the end of the engagement.

3. What the grant does not include. The Licensee may not distribute this runtime separately from
   the suite it was delivered in, sublicense it, offer it as a service to third parties, or use it to
   run programs other than those migrated for the Licensee by Katana, without a further written
   agreement with the copyright holder.

4. Provenance. Each delivered copy carries the version of Katana that produced it and the hash of the
   dialect profile the proof was made under (docs/PROFILE.md). The proof report delivered with the
   suite states what was proven and what was not (docs/PROOF.md); this license grants no warranty
   beyond what that report states.

5. Notices. The Licensee keeps this notice and the copyright notice in every copy.

6. No warranty beyond the proof report. Except as stated in the proof report delivered with the
   suite, this runtime is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, and the copyright holder is
   not liable for damages arising from its use.

Status: DRAFT. Written by Fable on 2026-10-05 from R-002; not legal advice; in force as the template
for rt/ once Ghost approves this file, and to be reviewed by counsel before the first delivery to a
customer. Until a Licensee is named in an engagement's schedule, section 2 grants nothing.
